    "turn_text": "welcome back to the show. Good morning. Thanks so much for listening. Happy Friday. Finally, time for a weekend. And it's going to be a beautiful weekend, too, by the way. The weather is going to be awesome. As long as we get through today, the wind out there is insane. And it's, it's like howling. It is so crazy. Weird, especially since the fact that it is Halloween and we're out there this morning. I mean, it's, it's just, it's Halloween, creepy wind. It really is. That should go through the day today. But it is going to be letting up going to be a nice weekend today, only a highest 65. What a change. But you know what, in my opinion, it's perfect, perfect for Halloween to have it just a little bit cooler. So the White House, they had their national climate advisor, Gina McCarthy. She ended up going on MSNBC's Haley Jackson reports show yesterday and was responding to the concerns that the increased regulations will cause increased gas and oil prices. When she was on the show, Haley Jackson had asked her that big oil hearing on Capitol Hill significant, frankly historic, that they're all coming together. There is sort of an argument that you've heard some Republicans make that more regulations could lead to higher gas in oil prices, et cetera. I wonder how you respond to that and your reaction to what you have been able to see so far related to this hearing that is still going on, by the way. McCarthy responds to that by saying, yeah, well, this is basically a day of reckoning. I think for the oil and gas sector, because for many decades, they denied climate change. And now that they're every day seeing the wildfires, the droughts, the floods, the heat stress, people no longer listening to listening to that or tolerating it. So they can't get away with that anymore. They have had to get serious about delivering clean energy and electricity to the people in this country. And they have to stop with the deception and move into the decade and help us make the transition to clean energy so that we can win the 21st century here. So there's no more hiding climate change. There's no more client deniers, climate deniers. And there's just about who wins the future and who addresses climate in the smartest way, which we intend to do It's going to be a big winner. I talk about on time how I think that progressivism and liberalism is kind of a mental disease. I think that climateism, that's a new word, I'm making it up, climateism, is also a level of mental disorder. It's people who latch on to everything climate. Everything has got to be climate for these people and it doesn't matter what it is. And of course, we've seen this. We have seen the oil companies and the fuel companies and energy companies. Granted, there are still some that are maybe not quite so there. But as a whole, our energy has become cleaner and cleaner and cleaner over the decades. And now this is something that I think we're all smart enough to know, that it's not going to be one of these, you make a mandate on Friday, and then by Monday everything has changed. But the climate nut bags that are out there, they refuse to look at the developments and where we have gone. And granted, yeah.",
