    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91353.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 54,
    "turn_text": "Glenn Yunken. Now, according to this new poll is leading McAuliffe by eight points as the election day comes up on Tuesday. That is a huge jump because as of just yesterday, it was only by 10th of a point. It is now taking a significant job in McAuliffe. He's been pulling out all the big Dems, big guns. He is brought in Obama. He's brought in Biden. He's brought in Bernie Sanders. And apparently he's not working out so well for him like he thought it would be. And this will be a huge upset for the Democrat party. if Glenn Yunken can actually take the governor's seat coming up on Tuesday. And the latest Fox News poll shows that young kids momentum has dramatically shifted over the course of two weeks, climbing up over five point deficit to take a commanding lead over McAuliffe. It's a 53 to 50 or 53 to 48% among likely voters. That is huge. And of course, Yunken, he is pledged to make sure that we get rid of, or they get rid of, critical race theory in the Virginia schools. And of course, the Loudoun County of Virginia, that situation with the schools has made such headlines and has really highlighted one of the big problems going on in Virginia. And of course, the Democrat, Terry McAuliffe, the former governor, who's running again, he's basically point playing said, hey, look, the school should have last say of what's going on with teaching your kids. And with everything going on in Loudon County, Virginia, right there that's making worldwide headlines, probably not the best statement to make. That's a statement that maybe you make that on Wednesday, the day after election. You know, not before that. But not looking good for McAuliffe as we're just days away from the actual election, trailing eight points to the Republican. And it's been a little while since there's been a Republican in charge of Virginia. So it'll be great to watch this. And of course, some other bad news for Terry McAuliffe. Imaging wise, somebody's gonna have a good stir in talking to you on this one, I'm sure. But the daughter of McAuliffe, Sally McAuliffe, along with a bunch of her friends, have showed off a photo that went viral, of them flashing the middle finger in front of the Republican headquarters, where there were signs for Glenn Yunken. Oh, Sally, Sally, that was, that was probably not a very good grown up moment. And I think dad's going to have to have a chat with you a little bit. But hey, you know, only Republicans are the, the vile mean, you know, people. Oh, wait a second. Why, why isn't they say that all the time? And then it ends up being the Dems that are doing it. that's what you gotta remember. If the Democrats are accusing you of doing something, we know that's exactly what they're doing. Hang on, we gotta break for news, we'll be right back.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_14",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
