    "turn_text": "welcome back to hour number two of the show. Good morning. Thanks so much for listening. Coming up next hour, by the way, we do have Congressman Neil Gunn is going to be joining us on the show. Want to talk with him about, man, for the most part, I want to talk to him about this Build Back Better mess. And everything else going on in Washington, what we're going to do about it. We're going to talk with him coming up next hour for that. So stick around for that. Oh, anyhow, the school system mass that is going on around this country. Like I said, it's going to be without a doubt the epicenter of the revolution in this country to turn things around. That's where it's all starting. And it's kind of great to see that parents have woke up to a lot of what's going on there. And of course, it's exposed a lot of things going on there as well. And I don't think there's a day that goes by now. that we are not hearing some sort of a story about something going on in a school board. And thankfully we haven't had much here. I've had a few things that have been said to me about a few programs that might be going on in our school. And you know what I think it's time for us to actually get somebody from the school board on. And maybe we'll do that, reach out to somebody from the school board and have them come talk to us about the school board here and what's going on. See what's happening. But Loudon County, Virginia, which again, the epicenter of the school board fiasco's where a lot of this is all being exposed. And we have seen the parent that got arrested a few weeks back for basically going up and saying, hey, my daughter was sexually assaulted in the bathroom and you guys are covering it up. And that became a big thing. And then there's parents that are complaining about the CRT and about the transgender bathrooms and everything else. And it has become mess after mess after mess for Loudon County. Really, truly, it's at a point where the citizens of Loudon County, Virginia, are wanting that school board to resign. And I think if the members of that school board were smart at this point, they should just do it. They should collectively all of them just go, whoa, okay, we're going to step aside and start it over. There's already some parents that have said, fine, you know what, this is what we're going to do. I'm going to run against you. And that's honestly one of the things you got to do. And I think that with this fiasco that we've had with the school system, school systems is showing that that is a powerful position where you can make a difference. You know, you always get those people that go, ah, you know what, you should run for office or I want to run for office. I'm not sure what I want to do. That's something to do. As we've learned that these school board clearly is a spot where you could make a huge difference. But in Loudoun County, the sheriff there is now investigating something new with the school system. And this is multiple incidents of inappropriate touching in the middle schools. A new investigation is underway in Loudon County, Virginia by the Sheriff's Department after multiple reported incidents of a male student touching other students inappropriately at a district middle school. The Loudon County Sheriff's Office reported yesterday that a school resource office learned from school personnel that on Wednesday, a male student had been inappropriately touched over his clothing by another male student in a hallway of Harmony Middle School. Now, this is also one of these things where you got to be careful on jumping to judgment audit, which is something that may be the case, but you just don't know until the investigation is over, but there is another investigation happening. The sheriff's office reported that at this time, the detectives had determined that there are additional male students who were inappropriately touched by the same individual. Those incidents may not be previously reported to the school officials or law enforcement. So the Loudon County Sheriff's Office is currently conducting follow-ups with school officials, witnesses, and parents. And the reports comes only two days after high school students in the scandal-ridden school district held a walkout to support other sexual assault victims. But apparently, the school system is covering up a lot of this stuff. And why? That's a good question. I mean, this is a mail-on-mail contact They covered up the story of a transgender boy going into, well, let me rephrase this, a boy claiming to be transgender goes into a girl's restroom and basically assaults, sexually assaults a ninth, ninth grade girl. And now we have obviously a male who's attracted other males touching other males in the school system covering it up. Now look, I say it all the time, I don't care about who loves who and what you, that doesn't mean anything to me. But there are certain things that regardless to the lifestyle that you live, the whatever the color of your skin is, whatever your gender is, whatever you think your gender is, you shouldn't be treated differently just because. So now that's another scandal that is going on in Loudon County. And we'll see if it ends up being another situation with that school department covering things up. It seems to be one thing after another. And you would think that teachers of all people would be the ones that would be the most compassionate for students and want to make sure that they take care of things and make sure that they're treated right. There's another story out now about a Florida school board member. who accompanied elementary school children on a field trip to a gay bar. I'm kidding. The Florida school board member reportedly accompanied elementary schools on a field trip out to this gay bar and said it was so honored to be invited to chaperone Wilton manners elementary field trip to the incredible rosies, which is a Broward County school board member Sarah Leonardo wrote in a Facebook post, which was reported by Fox news. The students and I had a fun walk over and learned a lot about our community. A huge thank you to Rosie's Bar and Grill for hosting this special field trip every year, every year. So it's not a new thing, but it's now being exposed. Photographs included in the Facebook posts show the elementary school students at Rosie's Bar and Grill, which is a gay bar in Wilton manners, Florida. And the post has since ignited a lot of outrage on social media outlets. and uh... you know it's even got the attention nationally of some of our politicians born up over who's the uh... the republican representative from colorado she said leave out everything early out everything else why in god's name are they bringing elementary school uh... kids to an establishment that aren't supposed to admit anyone under twenty one And that right there is actually the argument that it should be. It shouldn't be whether or not it was a gay bar or not a gay bar or whatever, but it's an establishment that you have to be 21 to get into. And this school on an annual basis, according to the post, has been bringing the kids there for a field trip. What kind of a lesson and message does that show? And even one of the parents that tweeted about this said exactly what I just said. The kind of bar is not even the point. It's a bar. It just makes you wonder what some of these teachers is like, what are you even thinking? John, that's funny. I don't know if that would get away with that, but that's funny. It's just, it's every day, every day there's another story when it comes to that. And I'm not done. I wish it. I wish I only had the two stories for the day, but I'm not done. California school board president gets caught on a live mic saying F you after hearing from a concerned parent. Yeah, these are the type of people that we have in our elected offices. People who think that they are so much better than you. You know, when you're in an elected position, you're going to hear a lot of good, you're going to hear a lot of bad. It just comes with the territory. And if you can't handle that, maybe you shouldn't be there. You're going to get criticism. As a matter of fact, as a politician, you're probably criticized more than anybody else. And that's part of the job. Because there's going to be somebody that's going to go, oh my God, Congressman Joe Smith, I love him. He's the greatest ever. And then there's going to be somebody else that's going to be standing right next to you and go, that guy is the biggest idiot on the planet. What are you talking about? He couldn't find his way to Washington, let alone do something there. It's always going to be that way. And you're always going to get criticized for something. It's a horrible job. I don't know why anybody does it. And I don't know why my friends keep asking me to do it again. It may be one day, but in the meantime, we're doing this. But the president of the California School Board is recorded on the live mic uttering the FU after her parent had raised the concerns over the mask mandates in class along with the vaccines for children. The parent who spoke during the school board meeting raised the concerns regarding those mandates and the vaccines for the kids just a couple of days ago at the Los Altamado school, a unified school district during their, their board of education meeting. And as her time came to a close, she attempted to finish the thought while the school board president, Marley Davis said, thank you, thank you, Margaret's next, thank you, your time's up. And in a moment of quiet, she uttered a few, which was picked up by her microphone. KTLATV reported that Davis had apologized for her remark after there were calls for her to resign as the school board's president. In her apology, she noted, when members of the public addressed the Board of Education, they must be held with respect. You think? But you only thought that after you got clocked though. You didn't think that before because can't believe this parent, a parent. You breeder can't believe you had the nerve to come up here to my board meeting and address me in that tone. Oh, how dare you? You peasant. Go back to making cookies or something, you breeder. I mean, that's that attitude that they have. And it's like, come on. And the mother ended up saying that, you know, Davidson, the school or president needs to step down. And after her true colors were shown, that's no taking that back. And you know what, this is great that parents are finally fighting this fight and doing that, because we got to keep doing this. We have got to make sure that we stop allowing this all to happen. 233-9988, that is the phone number for the show this morning. Good morning. Welcome to the Brian Rush Show.",
