    "turn_text": "Oh, yeah, you know, that's that's that's probably more than what we actually need to say. You know, but it but it is definitely time for for probably an impeachment on that one. I mean, we you got to be very careful when you say that way because, you know, the there's certain people that don't take kindly to it. If you know what I mean. But You know, this, this administration is a disaster. It really, truly is an absolute disaster. And the administration needs to be stopped and it needs to be stopped the right way. We need to have very strong leaders in our politics to stop it. They need to, even the Democrats at this point need to stop this Build Back Better Build. Even a downsized version of it is not good. There's a lot of problems with this bill. And of course, the other one that we're seeing and we've heard about was the IRS reporting provision in the bill. This is the one where they're going to give the IRS incredible powers to come after us and to look after you. And remember, as Joe Biden said, this plan isn't going to cost anything. This bill is absolutely nothing whatsoever. And of course, we're finding out if that was the case, then why is it that the rich are going to pay for things? Why is it that we now have to have the IRS be able to look at individuals and $600 or more in annual transactions? And of course, this is something that got confusing at first. They were talking about how with the $600 transaction. We all thought, oh, well, if you made a transaction of $600 or more that the FBI or the IRS would have the ability to look at you. That's not the case. It's annual transactions. So if you over the course of a year, and of course they've changed that number from $600,000 to $10,000, if you do that many insurance actions that the IRS automatically will have the right to be able to check out your bank account. We'll be able to look into your account, see what it is that you're doing. Now think about that. If you rent an apartment right now, pretty much anywhere in Bay County, it's about $1,000 a month. If you have a mortgage, It could be also in that area of $1,000 a month, maybe a little bit more. So just for your rent or your mortgage, you will still exceed $10,000 in annual transactions. And that doesn't include the Starbucks coffee that you buy, the gas that you buy, the movie you go to see, the dinner you go to see. You think about all of the transactions that you will be spending over the year is going to weigh over $10,000. So basically, this bill is going to allow the IRS to look into every single American's bank account for what? And sadly, they admitted for what? The administration said to make sure that everybody is paying their taxes. They want to make sure that you're not getting some cash payments in place and doing some underground deals and not paying your fair share. It's no longer about the millionaires and the billionaires paying their fair share. It's you. You who do $10,000, let's originally keep it at the $600. So if you had $600 or transactions or more, which is virtually every American that has any money, that we want to make sure you're paying your fair share. Joe Biden came out and said that. But don't worry about it because the Build Back Better Plan, zero cost of the taxpayers. You're not, you're not gonna pay a dime. This isn't gonna cost anything. $3.5 trillion for the price tag, but you're not gonna pay for it. Really, who is? The taxpayers are gonna, well, we are the taxpayers. I mean, the rich, well, the rich doesn't have enough money and they're not gonna do it. Then, well, you know, we're gonna look at your, we're gonna make sure you're paying your taxes. And they're also adding another $78 billion, $78 billion going into supersizing the IRS auditing. So not only are they going to be able to go after you for having $10,000 worth of transactions in a year, but now they're going to be funded to do so. Keep in mind the IRS right now, they are still like processing tax returns from like two, three, four years ago. And now they're going to increase their auditing capability to be able to come after more of us to make sure that we're paying our fair share. This is all the stuff that we're looking at with a Build Back Better plan. I said many times before that the What is that plan? The SB1, the For The People Act, was the most dangerous bill to ever pass the house. And it is. Build Back Better Act is right there neck and neck with the most dangerous. The two of them are the most dangerous bills to ever pass because it will fundamentally change America. And that's not me saying that. That is Joe Biden who said this. He said this yesterday that when we get all of this past, it will fundamentally change America. Let that sink in. They are ready now and they are opposed to change the country that we know. And the way that they want to change it is they want a socialist country. And both of those bills Granite before the people bill has been completely shot down. But every time you turn around, elements of that bill are being put into other bills. They will fundamentally change this country into a socialist country. If we don't stop it. That's why you have to, you got to call every senator in the state, every senator in the neighboring state, every congressman, every congresswoman. and let them know, knock it off. Hey God, we gotta take a break, we'll be right back. Congressman Neil Dunn gonna be joining us after the top of the hour, hang on, we'll be right back.",
