    "turn_text": "some great work. I mean, I do love the medical topics. I've done some great work on research and treatments of cancer, specifically prostate cancer, but a lot of other cancers as well. And development of radiopharmaceutical industry, which was a niche interest of mine as well before I got here. We do think that we could probably going to have to legislate something on this natural immunity that you mentioned earlier. the T-cell community, we've got to get people to understand that it is good, it's strong, it's robust, it's durable, and so we want Medicare to reimburse that testing, and we want people to recognize that as a standard of medical practice. And then we want to reign in NIH. We don't want them to ever again go out and do gain-of-function research. It's certainly not anywhere, not in China, maybe not anywhere at all. And we have a long history of of lab leaks, leaks of accidents and infectious disease labs around the world, including right here in America. You will recall the anthrax scares a few",
